            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral transversus abdominis plane block for managing pain after a pancreas transplant.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>277-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report the first clinical application of a bilateral transversus abdominis plane block for treating pain after a pancreas transplant. In this case, a 36-year-old chronic opioid user presented postoperatively with severe incisional pain following a pancreas transplant. The pain was not ameliorated with opioids and was successfully treated with the administration of bilateral transversus abdominis plane blocks with 0.5% ropivicaine. Pain relief lasted for 6 hours.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
